73 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 185 0 R
/E (The Challenge: The cozy, pastoral nature of some solarpunk fiction \(like using pedal-powered wagons and bicycles\) is often antithetical to globalization and large-scale economies. If long-distance travel takes too long, supply chains for advanced components \(like graphene batteries\) collapse, forcing society back into uncomfortable, hard agricultural labor just to survive.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [33]
>>
endobj
74 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 186 0 R
/E (The Counter-Argument: The pastoral undertone might be a prerequisite for maintaining a strict solarpunk aesthetic. These worlds often function best when imagining smaller human enclaves where everything is produced and served locally, or on smaller geographic scales \(like a small moon\) where massive shipping distances aren't required.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [34]
>>
endobj
